@JwtAuthApi_HostAddress = http://localhost:5274

### Endpoint público (sin token): productos sin precio
GET {{JwtAuthApi_HostAddress}}/api/products/public
Accept: application/json

### Login -> devuelve access_token y refresh_token
# @name login
POST {{JwtAuthApi_HostAddress}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "admin",
  "password": "Admin123!"
}

### Endpoint protegido usando el access token del login (incluye el precio)
GET {{JwtAuthApi_HostAddress}}/api/products
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.access_token}}

### Usuario autenticado (claims del token)
GET {{JwtAuthApi_HostAddress}}/api/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.access_token}}

### Crear producto (solo rol Admin)
POST {{JwtAuthApi_HostAddress}}/api/products
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Tablet",
  "description": "10 pulgadas",
  "price": 199.99
}

### Refresh -> rota el par de tokens
POST {{JwtAuthApi_HostAddress}}/api/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refresh_token": "{{login.response.body.refresh_token}}"
}

### Logout -> revoca el refresh token (no requiere access token)
POST {{JwtAuthApi_HostAddress}}/api/auth/logout
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refresh_token": "{{login.response.body.refresh_token}}"
}

### Health check
GET {{JwtAuthApi_HostAddress}}/health

###
